At this stage, you basically want to make yourself as strong as you can before
tackling Gehennom and the endgame, and there's very little danger. How long you
spend at this stage is entirely up to you, but for a first ascenscion it pays
to be thorough.

When you're a wizard, a wish for a spellbook or a scroll is a wasted wish. Wish
for a magic marker, and write blessed charging. If you haven't already recharged
your current markers, do so. Use markers to ride a spellbook of identify first,
then magic mapping, detect treasure, remove curse and whatever other spells you
need.

You'll want a t-shirt (you can get one polypiling normal armors with a little
patience), gauntlets of dexterity, and a helm of brilliance (or a cornuthaum).
Enchant and fooproof all your armor as high as you can, wishing for magic
markers as-needed. Spend leftover wishes on artifacts (which you may or may
not succeed in getting), such as the Eyes of the Overworld and the Orb of Fate.

Cast detect treasure on each level and loot any vaults you find, as well as
Ludios. Then find a non-coaligned priest, donate for protection until you have
no gold left, then (carefully) kill the priest. Take the gold and repeat on
another, doing any coaligned priest last (and not killing it). Remember there's
a priest of moloch in the valley of the dead.

Finally, gather up all your potions, cancel everything that's not either full
healing, gain level, or an ingredient which can be turned into one of those
through alchemy. Bless them, and start polypiling, keeping anything that can
be turned into FH or GL. Mix the potions, drink lots of FH, and your max HP
will enter quadruple digits.

